## Short answer  
No – you didn’t miss a step.  
MapLibre GL JS was forked from **Mapbox GL JS v1.13**, not from the v2 line that introduced `map.setFog()`, `map.getFreeCameraOptions()`, `map.setFreeCameraOptions()`, etc. Those APIs simply **don’t exist in MapLibre**.  

Instead you have to use the **MapLibre equivalents** (or rewrite the logic) that were added later in the MapLibre code-base:

| Mapbox v2 feature | MapLibre replacement | How to use it |
|-------------------|----------------------|---------------|
| `map.setFog({...})` (and the `fog` root-level style object) | **`map.setSky({...})`** and the `sky` root-level style object | `map.setSky({ "sky-color": "#199EF3", "horizon-color": "#fff", "fog-color": "#cce", "fog-ground-blend": 0.5, … })` |
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` / `map.setFreeCameraOptions()` (FreeCameraOptions class) | **Camera-options helpers** – `map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(...)` (or `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) + `map.jumpTo() / map.easeTo() / map.flyTo()` | ```js\nconst cam = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation([lng, lat], altitude, bearing, pitch, roll);\nmap.easeTo(cam);\n``` |
| `map.setFreeCameraOptions({position, orientation, ...})` | Same as above – compute a `CameraOptions` object and pass it to `jumpTo`, `easeTo` or `flyTo`. | See example below. |

Everything else (markers, popups, controls, source/layer APIs, events, expressions, etc.) works unchanged after you swap the package, namespace, token, and style URL.

Below is a **complete “what-to-do” checklist** plus concrete code snippets so you can finish the migration without hunting for missing methods.

---

## 1. Install / upgrade MapLibre

```bash
# Remove the old package (optional but clean)
npm uninstall mapbox-gl

# Install the current MapLibre release (v6.x as of 2026-07-22)
npm install maplibre-gl
```

> **Note:** v6 ships **ES-modules only** – there is no UMD bundle or default export. If you still need a UMD build you must pin to v5.x, but the recommended path is to move to the ES-module API.

---

## 2. Update imports & CSS

```js
// BEFORE (Mapbox)
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css';

// AFTER (MapLibre v6)
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';   // or: import {Map, NavigationControl} from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';
```

If you load from a CDN, replace the script tag with a module import:

```html
<link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';
  // your map code goes here …
</script>
```

---

## 3. Swap the namespace everywhere

```js
// BEFORE
const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ … });
new mapboxgl.Marker().addTo(map);
map.addControl(new mapboxgl.NavigationControl());

// AFTER
const map = new maplibregl.Map({ … });
new maplibregl.Marker().addTo(map);
map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl());
```

Also rename any CSS class selectors you wrote manually:

* `mapboxgl-ctrl` → `maplibregl-ctrl`
* `mapboxgl-popup` → `maplibregl-popup`
* etc.

---

## 4. Remove the Mapbox access token

```js
// DELETE this line – MapLibre does not read mapboxgl.accessToken
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.ey...';
```

If you need a token for a third-party tile service (e.g., MapTiler, Mapbox-compatible tiles), pass it **as part of the source URL** or via the service’s own configuration object, not on the global `maplibregl` object.

---

## 5. Provide a non-Mapbox style URL

Mapbox-style URLs (`mapbox://styles/...`) will 404 in MapLibre. Choose one of the following:

| Option | Example URL | When to use |
|--------|-------------|-------------|
| **OpenFreeMap** (free, no key) | `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` | Quick sanity-check; works out-of-the-box |
| **MapTiler Cloud** (requires API key) | `https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets/style.json?key=YOUR_KEY` | If you already have a MapTiler account |
| **Self-hosted style** (PMTiles, Martin, tileserver-gl) | `https://mydomain.com/tiles/style.json` | Production, full control |
| **Custom-converted Mapbox style** | Export from Mapbox Studio → edit source URLs → host yourself | If you love a style you built in Mapbox Studio |

```js
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // <-- change this
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});
```

If you want to keep a style you designed in Mapbox Studio, **export the JSON**, replace every `source` that looks like `mapbox://...` with the URL of your new vector source, and adjust `source-layer` names if they differ. Tools that help:

* **Maputnik** – visual editor for MapLibre styles.
* **@maplibre/maplibre-gl-style-spec** – CLI validator (`npx gl-style-validate style.json`).

---

## 6. Replace v2-only APIs

### 6.1 Fog → Sky

```js
// Mapbox v2
map.setFog({
  'color': '#f8f4f0',
  'high-color': '#add8e6',
  'space-color': '#d8f2ff',
  'horizon-blend': 0.3
});
```

```js
// MapLibre (v6+)
map.setSky({
  'sky-color': '#f8f4f0',
  'horizon-color': '#add8e6',
  'fog-color': '#d8f2ff',
  'fog-ground-blend': 0.5,
  'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
  'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
  'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
});
```

*The `sky` object lives at the root of the style JSON (`"sky": { … }`) just like `fog` did.*

### 6.2 Free-camera options → CameraOptions helpers

Mapbox v2 let you set an arbitrary 3-D camera:

```js
map.setFreeCameraOptions({
  position: [lng, lat, altitude],
  orientation: { pitch: 45, bearing: 30, roll: 0 }
});
```

MapLibre does **not** have a `FreeCameraOptions` class. Instead:

```js
// 1️⃣ Compute a CameraOptions object from the same parameters
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  [lng, lat],          // lng/lat
  altitude,            // altitude in meters
  bearing,             // bearing (°)
  pitch,               // pitch (°)
  roll                  // roll (°) – supported from v5.0.0
);

// 2️⃣ Move the map – choose the animation you like
map.easeTo(camOpts);   // smooth animated move
// or
map.jumpTo(camOpts);   // instant
// or
map.flyTo(camOpts);    // “fly” animation
```

If you need a **look-at** (camera from point A looking at point B) you can use the older helper:

```js
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromTo(
  [fromLng, fromLat], fromAltitude,
  [toLng,   toLat],   toAltitude
);
map.easeTo(camOpts);
```

Both helpers are part of the **MapLibre API** (v5+). They return a plain `CameraOptions` object that you pass to any of the standard camera methods (`jumpTo`, `easeTo`, `flyTo`).

---

## 7. Plugins & extra services

| Feature | Mapbox plugin | MapLibre status / alternative |
|---------|---------------|------------------------------|
| **Geocoder UI** | `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` | Works unchanged *if* you only use the UI component. The underlying API calls must be swapped (see §8). |
| **Directions UI** | `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-directions` | No official MapLibre fork. Use a UI wrapper around OSRM/OpenRouteService or MapTiler Directions. |
| **GeolocateControl** | built-in | Still works (`new maplibregl.GeolocateControl()`). |
| **Clustered point layers** | built-in | Same API (`cluster: true` in source). |
| **Custom controls** | any `mapboxgl.Control` implementation | Rename the class to extend `maplibregl.Control` (or just implement the same three methods: `onAdd`, `onRemove`). |

The definitive list of compatible plugins lives in the community-maintained repo:

**👉 https://github.com/maplibre/awesome-maplibre**

Search there for each Mapbox plugin you use; many have been forked (e.g., `maplibre-gl-geocoder`) or have a drop-in replacement.

---

## 8. Replace Mapbox web services (Geocoding, Directions, etc.)

MapLibre is just the rendering engine; it does **not** provide hosted APIs. You must point your code at open or commercial alternatives.

| Mapbox service | Open-source / free alternative | Commercial / hosted alternative |
|----------------|-------------------------------|---------------------------------|
| **Geocoding / search** | Nominatim (OSM), Photon, Pelias | MapTiler Geocoding, OpenCage, LocationIQ |
| **Directions / routing** | OSRM demo (no SLA), OpenRouteService, Valhalla | MapTiler Directions, GraphHopper, Mapbox Directions (if you keep a token) |
| **Static maps** | TileServer-GL, TileServer-PHP, MapLibre Static API (self-host) | MapTiler Static Maps, Cloudflare Images, etc. |

**Example: Nominatim search**

```js
async function search(query) {
  const resp = await fetch(`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`);
  const data = await resp.json(); // GeoJSON FeatureCollection
  return data;
}

// Use the result to add a marker
search('Golden Gate Bridge').then(fc => {
  const feature = fc.features[0];
  new maplibregl.Marker()
    .setLngLat(feature.geometry.coordinates)
    .addTo(map);
});
```

If you need higher-throughput or guaranteed uptime, spin up your own Nominatim/OSRM instance or subscribe to a managed provider (MapTiler, Pelias-as-a-service, etc.).

---

