Below is a quick-reference guide that shows **all the practical ways you can add a search / geocoder box to a map that is built with Mapbox GL JS v2**.  
It’s split into three sections:

| Section | What it gives you | When you’d pick it | Quick-start code |
|---------|-------------------|--------------------|-------------------|
| **1️⃣ Official Mapbox Geocoder** | Fully-featured UI, autocomplete, biasing, “use-my-location”, address-type filtering, built-in results-to-Mapbox-GL-JS integration. | You already have a Mapbox access token and you’re happy to stay on the Mapbox platform (tiles, styles, APIs). | `new MapboxGeocoder({ accessToken: MAPBOX_TOKEN, mapboxgl: mapboxgl })` |
| **2️⃣ Open-source “MapLibre-GL-Geocoder” (or other community plugins)** | Same UI component, but you can point it at any HTTP geocoding service (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, OpenCage, etc.). | You want to keep the Mapbox GL JS v2 map but avoid the Mapbox geocoding service (cost, licensing, or you already have another provider). | `new MapLibreGeocoder({ query: '', placeholder: 'Search…', getItemValue: … })` |
| **3️⃣ DIY “fetch-and-render” approach** | Full control over UI, request format, result handling, and styling. | You have a custom UI library (React, Vue, Svelte, plain HTML) or you need a very specific look/behaviour that the ready-made widgets don’t give. | `fetch('https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?...').then(r=>r.json()).then(showResults)` |

Below each section you’ll find:

* **Why you’d choose it** (cost, licensing, feature set, ease of use).  
* **What you need to add** (npm package, CSS, API key).  
* **A minimal, copy-and-paste example** that works with Mapbox GL JS v2 (ES-module or UMD).  
* **Gotchas & migration notes** (especially if you later decide to move to MapLibre GL JS).

---

## 1️⃣ Official Mapbox Geocoder (MapboxGeocoder)

### When to use it
* You already have a **Mapbox access token** (free tier or paid).  
* You want the **tightest integration** – the widget automatically adds a marker, fits the map to the result, and can bias results to the current viewport.  
* You need **premium features** like *autocomplete ranking*, *address-type filtering*, *proximity bias*, or *Mapbox-specific address components* (e.g., “place”, “postcode”).  

### What you need
| Item | How to get it |
|------|---------------|
| **npm package** | `npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` |
| **CSS** | `import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';` |
| **Mapbox token** | `mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.ey...';` (or pass it in the constructor) |

> **Note:** The widget works with **Mapbox GL JS v2** (the proprietary license version) **without any code changes**. It also works with MapLibre GL JS v2+ if you give it a `mapboxgl` reference, but you’ll still need a Mapbox token for the geocoding service.

### Minimal example (ES-module)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Mapbox GL JS v2 + MapboxGeocoder</title>
  <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
    .geocoder { position:absolute; z-index:1; width:50%; left:10px; top:10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<div id="geocoder" class="geocoder"></div>

<script type="module">
  import mapboxgl from 'https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.js';
  import MapboxGeocoder from 'https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.js';

  // 1️⃣ Set your token
  mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.eyYOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN';

  // 2️⃣ Initialise the map
  const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
    center: [-122.44, 37.76],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // 3️⃣ Add the geocoder UI
  const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
    accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
    mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // <-- important for the built-in marker handling
    placeholder: 'Search places…',
    marker: true                 // automatically add a marker at the result
  });

  // 4️⃣ Insert it into the DOM
  document.getElementById('geocoder').appendChild(geocoder.onAdd(map));

  // Optional: listen to the result event
  geocoder.on('result', e => console.log('Result:', e.result));
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key options you can tweak

| Option | Description | Example |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `proximity` | Bias results toward a lon/lat (e.g., user location). | `{ proximity: { longitude: -122.42, latitude: 37.78 } }` |
| `bbox` | Restrict results to a bounding box. | `{ bbox: [-123, 37, -121, 38] }` |
| `types` | Limit to `address`, `place`, `postcode`, etc. | `{ types: 'address,place' }` |
| `countries` | ISO-3166-1 alpha-2 country filter. | `{ countries: 'us,ca' }` |
| `placeholder` | UI placeholder text. | `{ placeholder: 'Search…' } |
| `marker` | `true` (default) adds a default marker; `false` disables it; you can also pass a custom `new mapboxgl.Marker()` instance. | `{ marker: false }` |
| `flyTo` | Controls the animation when a result is selected. | `{ flyTo: { speed: 1.2 } }` |

### Gotchas

* **Rate limits** – Free tier: 100 k requests/month, 600 req/min. Exceeding it returns HTTP 429.  
* **Token leakage** – If you embed the token in client-side code, treat it as a **public token** (only the “public” scopes are allowed). Never embed a secret token.  
* **Styling** – The widget ships with its own CSS. You can override it by targeting `.mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder` and its children.  
* **Future migration** – If you later switch to MapLibre GL JS, you can keep the same widget **as long as you keep a Mapbox token** (the geocoder talks to Mapbox’s API, not to the map library). If you want to drop Mapbox entirely, move to option 2 or 3.

---

## 2️⃣ Open-source “MapLibre-GL-Geocoder” (or other community plugins)

### Why you might want it
* **No Mapbox token required** – you can point the widget at any HTTP geocoder (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, OpenCage, etc.).  
* **BSD-3-Clause license** – compatible with commercial projects.  
* **Works with both Mapbox GL JS v2 and MapLibre GL JS** (just pass the `mapboxgl` reference).  
* **Lightweight** – ~12 KB gzipped, no extra Mapbox SDK dependencies.

### Packages you can use

| Package | Repo | Typical geocoder back-ends |
|---------|------|----------------------------|
| `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder` | <https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder> | Any HTTP geocoder you configure (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, OpenCage). |
| `mapbox-gl-geocoder` (forked) | <https://github.com/zakjan/mapbox-gl-geocoder> | Same API as the official Mapbox widget but **no Mapbox token required** – you must supply a custom `geocoder` function. |
| `@geocoder-ol/geocoder` (OpenLayers) – not relevant for Mapbox GL. | — | — |

The **officially maintained** one is `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`. It ships with a tiny UI that mirrors the Mapbox widget, but you provide a **`geocoder` function** that returns a `Promise` of GeoJSON features.

### Install

```bash
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
# optional: a CSS reset if you don’t want the default styling
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css
```

### Minimal example using **OpenStreetMap Nominatim** (public demo endpoint – **do not use in production**)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Mapbox GL JS v2 + MapLibre-GL-Geocoder (Nominatim)</title>
  <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link href="node_modules/@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
    .geocoder { position:absolute; top:10px; left:10px; z-index:1; width:300px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<div id="geocoder" class="geocoder"></div>

<script type="module">
  import mapboxgl from 'https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.js';
  import { MapLibreGeocoder } from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';

  // 1️⃣ Initialise the map (any Mapbox style works – you still need a token for the tiles)
  mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.eyYOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN';
  const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
    center: [-122.44, 37.76],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // 2️⃣ Build a tiny wrapper around Nominatim
  const nominatimGeocoder = (query) => {
    const url = new URL('https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search');
    url.search = new URLSearchParams({
      q: query,
      format: 'geojson',
      addressdetails: 1,
      limit: 5,
    });
    return fetch(url)
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(data => ({
        // The geocoder expects an object with a `features` array (GeoJSON FeatureCollection)
        type: 'FeatureCollection',
        features: data.features.map(f => ({
          // Keep the geometry as-is
          geometry: f.geometry,
          // Add a human-readable `place_name` property (used by the UI)
          properties: {
            place_name: f.properties.display_name,
            // optional: you can add `text` and `place_type` for richer UI
            text: f.properties.name || f.properties.display_name,
            place_type: ['address']
          }
        }))
      }));
  };

  // 3️⃣ Initialise the geocoder widget
  const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
    maplibregl: mapboxgl,
